         This game is AWESOME.  The AI is incredible.  I love the way your creature learns things(bahaha, master fisher!).  Your actions really do have impact on the world, and your creature has a mind of his own.  My |_33+ tiger is kind, and he'll pick up villagers and tickle them, supply them with wood and grain, cast miracles(he has to watch all this happen, and he'll try it till he succeeds <img src="images/smilies/smile.gif" border=0>).  The combat interface isnt bad, but it isnt great either.  The spells are awesome though, and if your creature watches you cast a certain miracle long enough, he'll learn how to as well.  Mine summons wheat, throws fireballs, summons wood, grows a forest, waters fields etc.  The people are hilarious, although their constant bitching makes me occasionally throw one out to sea.  You also have to teach da creature right and wrong.  I.E. the first time my tiger got hungry, he grabbed a villager and ate it.  I beat him within an inch of his life, and he never did it again.  Sure i felt bad (they cry and stuff <img src="images/smilies/frown.gif" border=0>) but i knew that i had to do it....ack i feel like a daddy.  You can also reward your creature for certain things, and he'll do them more often.  I.E. my creature eats a pig and i pet him till he's at 100% happiness.  He currently has a pork fetish <img src="images/smilies/biggrin.gif" border=0>.  The villagers can learn to love you, or fear you, and either way they will worship.  <br>
      Trying to impress a new village to worship you can be done in various ways.  From summoning them wood/grain, throwing things near them(cows, rocks, your creatures poop) or even throwing them proves yourself to them.  Which makes sense, you're obviously a god if you're magically picking someone up and throwing them into other people.  It really IS a cool game, the graphics are stunning, the controls take getting used to, but are perfect once you learn them, the fun factor is a 10 out of 10.  Mistah say: YOU BUY DIS NOW!!!<br>
